   "local_id": "ana_nonlinear_recovery",
   "name": {
    "extraction_status": "extracted",
    "value": "Analysis 1 – ALC rates of change in regional volumes over all APs (AP1-AP2-AP3)",
    "value_source": "reported",
    "evidence": {
     "status": "present",
     "sets": [
      {
       "source": "model_quote",
       "spans": [
        {
         "text": "Analysis 1 – ALC rates of change in regional volumes over all APs (AP1-AP2-AP3; see Table 2 and Supplementary Figure 1 )",
         "start_char": 21853,
         "end_char": 21973
        }
       ]
      }
     ]
    }
   },
   "definition": {
    "extraction_status": "extracted",
    "value": "ALC showed significant volume increases in frontal, parietal, occipital, and total cortical GM, cerebellum and thalamus over 7.5-months of abstinence, with a significant negative quadratic slope indicating different rates of regional volume change between AP1-AP2 than between AP2-AP3.",
    "value_source": "reported",
    "evidence": {
     "status": "present",
     "sets": [
      {
       "source": "model_quote",
       "spans": [
        {
         "text": "Given there were no significant effects for smoking status or smoking status x months abstinent interactions, the positive slopes for the linear term for months abstinent indicated that the ALC group showed significant volume increases in frontal, parietal, occipital, and total cortical GM, cerebellum and thalamus over 7.5-months of abstinence. The significant negative slope (i.e., “frowning” parabola) of the quadratic term for months abstinent in the above GM regions indicated ALC showed different rates of regional volume change between AP1-AP2 than between AP2-AP3.",
         "start_char": 22936,
         "end_char": 23509
        }
       ]
      }
     ]
    }
   },
   "prespecification": {
    "extraction_status": "extracted",
    "value": "hypothesis-driven",
    "value_source": "reported",
    "evidence": {
     "status": "present",
     "sets": [
      {
       "source": "model_quote",
       "spans": [
        {
         "text": "We predicted that:",
         "start_char": 6860,
         "end_char": 6878
        }
       ]
      }
     ]
    }
   },
   "interpretations": {
    "extraction_status": "extracted",
    "value": [
     "The primary findings from this study are: (1) ALC (both nsALC and sALC) showed significant volume increases in all GM and WM regions over approximately 7.5-months of abstinence, except the temporal GM and the lenticular nucleus, as well as decreased ventricular volume over 7.5-months;",
     "Rates of volume change for regional GM were significantly greater over 1-week to 1-month of abstinence than over 1 to 7.5-months of abstinence; linear WM volume changes were observed in ALC over 7.5 months."
    ],
    "value_source": "reported",
    "evidence": {
     "status": "present",
     "sets": [
      {
       "source": "model_quote",
       "spans": [
        {
         "text": "The primary findings from this study are: (1) ALC (both nsALC and sALC) showed significant volume increases in all GM and WM regions over approximately 7.5-months of abstinence, except the temporal GM and the lenticular nucleus, as well as decreased ventricular volume over 7.5-months; medical, psychiatric, and substance misuse comorbidities were not significant predictors of regional volume change.",
